      "created_at": "2025-07-25T21:19:17Z",
      "updated_at": "2025-07-25T21:19:17Z",
      "body": "> Since we haven't received any complaints since it regressed, and a fix I think would be difficult, IMO we should just delete the test, basically WONTFIXing [#2430](https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/2430).\n\nI would like to submit a complaint :) We [set a warning filter](https://github.com/BerkeleyLearnVerify/Scenic/blob/3e1f13608c5f230f6879036e3cd7c88475146536/src/scenic/core/vectors.py#L46) in one of our modules to suppress warnings from a 3rd-party library (scipy), and it's quite annoying that the warnings still show up when we run our test suite. When I first looked into this a couple of years ago, I saw #2430 was closed, so I assumed there was something specific to our setup causing the problem. But I've been revisiting it recently, and I think the problem is indeed caused by the fix to #3251 that you mention above.\n\n(I'll mention that I'm actually hoping for scipy to add an option to not emit the warnings in question in the first place; if that happens, then this issue would no longer bother us. But of course it might come up again with some other 3rd-party library.)",
